WebGPU: GPU timer results in the browser

A device the page created reaches bgfx through emscripten_webgpu_get_device, which imports it into no instance:
emdawnwebgpu queues the callbacks of its objects under the null instance. bgfx waits for the timer readback with
an AllowProcessEvents callback and calls wgpuInstanceProcessEvents on the instance it created itself, so the
callback never ran, the readback stayed pending, and no timer query was resolved again: every GPU time stayed 0.
In the browser the callback is now spontaneous; the page has one thread, so it runs from the event loop, between
frames.

diff --git a/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp b/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
--- a/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
@@ -6996,6 +6996,14 @@ WGPU_IMPORT
 		m_resolved   = false;
 		m_mapPending = true;
 
+		// In the browser a device the page created belongs to no instance: wgpuInstanceProcessEvents on bgfx's
+		// own instance never runs its callbacks. The page has one thread, so a spontaneous callback runs from the
+		// event loop, between frames.
+		const WGPUCallbackMode callbackMode = BX_ENABLED(BX_PLATFORM_EMSCRIPTEN)
+			? WGPUCallbackMode_AllowSpontaneous
+			: WGPUCallbackMode_AllowProcessEvents
+			;
+
 		WGPU_CHECK(wgpuBufferMapAsync(
 			  m_readback
 			, WGPUMapMode_Read
@@ -7003,7 +7011,7 @@ WGPU_IMPORT
 			, size_t(getBufferSize() )
 			, {
 				.nextInChain = NULL,
-				.mode        = WGPUCallbackMode_AllowProcessEvents,
+				.mode        = callbackMode,
 				.callback    = readTimestampResultsCb,
 				.userdata1   = this,
 				.userdata2   = NULL,
